   "text": "I read the drawing in pieces and joined them into one SMILES.\n\n- **Left end:** a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl group sits on the nitrogen of an isoindolin-1-one. The alkyne is on the benzene carbon next to the CH2-bearing ring-fusion carbon.\n- **Linker:** the alkyne is followed by five CH2 groups and then a C(=O) that acylates the ring nitrogen. That gives an 8-carbon chain including the carbonyl.\n- **Central bicycle:** an 8-membered ring (N, CH2, CH2, CH, N, C=O, CH, CH2) fused to a pyrrolidine through the shared CH and N.\n- **Benzothiophene amide:** the NH on the 8-membered ring carries a benzothiophene-2-carbonyl. The benzothiophene has a CF2\u2013P(=O)(OH)2 group at position 5.\n- **Right-hand side chain:** the pyrrolidine carboxamide NH is attached to a CH bearing a CH2CH2C(=O)NH2 chain and a thiazol-2-yl ring. The thiazole carries a 3,4-difluorophenyl group at position 4.\n\nStereochemistry comes only from the wedged bonds. I assigned CIP labels from the drawing and matched each to the @/@@ order in the SMILES:\n\n- NH-bearing carbon of the 8-membered ring: S\n- Ring-fusion CH: R\n- Pyrrolidine CH bearing the carboxamide: S\n- Side-chain CH bearing the thiazole: S\n\nThe glutarimide CH is drawn with plain bonds, so it has no stereo label.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CCC(N2Cc3c(C2=O)cccc3C#CCCCCCC(=O)N2C[C@H](NC(=O)c3cc4cc(C(F)(F)P(=O)(O)O)ccc4s3)C(=O)N3[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(N)=O)c4nc(cs4)-c4ccc(F)c(F)c4)CC[C@@H]3CC2)C(=O)N1"
